#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186198651 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186198417 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "2bfe2e3e-9d7b-5c53-8de8-2717237d3e9c" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating the Radius of Gyration of a Uniform Rectangular Laminar"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "06aa15d2-30ee-5cc9-b5dd-ac324e05cd6b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\sqrt{\\frac{17}{3}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186278654} {:answer/id #uuid "240de7aa-73fc-57f0-b478-71f4546ac6b0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\sqrt{\\frac{19}{3}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186278914} {:answer/id #uuid "578364b4-8440-58d4-999a-e71df76621b9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\sqrt{\\frac{16}{3}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186279394} {:answer/id #uuid "8474f088-76e4-5da5-a9e4-54e62eda057e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\sqrt{\\frac{13}{3}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186279781} {:answer/id #uuid "8f9f0418-d641-5bc4-9599-2fdec0a94b81" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\sqrt{5}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186279869}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "06aa15d2-30ee-5cc9-b5dd-ac324e05cd6b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\sqrt{\\frac{17}{3}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186278654} :answer-field/id #uuid "2413e5c4-0b04-5b4f-a226-389f725261b9" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186280894}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "5e1eb104-83e6-5dc7-913b-3996107f92c0" :question/math-academy-id "q-163011" :question/problem "A rectangular plate of mass $M$ and uniform mass density occupies the region\n$D=\\{(x,y)\\,:\\,0\\le x\\le 2,\\,\\,1\\le y\\le 3\\}.$ Find the radius of gyration of the plate about the origin." :question/worked-solution "For a plane lamina in the shape of a region $D$ with mass $M$ and mass density function $\\lambda (x,y),$ we have the following definitions:\n\n- The radius of gyration ${R}_{x}$ about the $x$-axis is given by\n${R}_{x}=\\sqrt{\\frac{{I}_{x}}{M}},$\nwhere ${I}_{x}$ is the moment of inertia about the $x$-axis.\n\n- The radius of gyration ${R}_{y}$ about the $y$-axis is given by\n${R}_{y}=\\sqrt{\\frac{{I}_{y}}{M}},$\nwhere ${I}_{y}$ is the moment of inertia about the $y$-axis.\n\n- The radius of gyration ${R}_{0}$ about the origin is given by\n${R}_{0}=\\sqrt{\\frac{{I}_{0}}{M}},$\nwhere ${I}_{0}$ is the moment of inertia about the origin.\n\nThe moment of inertia about the origin is defined as\n\n$$\n{I}_{0}={∬}_{D}\\lambda (x,y)({x}^{2}+{y}^{2})\\,\\text{d}A,\n$$\n\nwhere $\\lambda (x,y)$ is the mass density function.\n\nThe area of the rectangular plate $D$ is $A=2\\cdot 2=4.$ Since the plate has uniform density, the mass density function is given by\n\n$$\n\\lambda (x,y)=\\frac{M}{A}=\\frac{M}{4}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the moment of inertia about the origin is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{I}_{0} & ={∬}_{D}\\lambda (x,y)({x}^{2}+{y}^{2})\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & =\\frac{M}{4}{\\int }_{1}^{3}{\\int }_{0}^{2}{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}\\,\\text{d}x\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & =\\frac{M}{4}{\\int }_{1}^{3}{[\\frac{1}{3}{x}^{3}+x{y}^{2}]}_{x=0}^{x=2}\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & =\\frac{M}{4}{\\int }_{1}^{3}\\frac{8}{3}+2{y}^{2}\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & =\\frac{M}{2}{\\int }_{1}^{3}\\frac{4}{3}+{y}^{2}\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & =\\frac{M}{2}{[\\frac{4}{3}y+\\frac{1}{3}{y}^{3}]}_{1}^{3} \\\\  & =\\frac{M}{2}(4+9-(\\frac{4}{3}+\\frac{1}{3})) \\\\  & =\\frac{M}{2}(13-\\frac{5}{3}) \\\\  & =\\frac{M}{2}\\cdot \\frac{34}{3} \\\\  & =\\frac{17M}{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally,\n\n$$\n{R}_{0}^{2}=\\frac{17}{3}\\,⇒\\,{R}_{0}=\\sqrt{\\frac{17}{3}}.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186281676 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186198417 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "2bfe2e3e-9d7b-5c53-8de8-2717237d3e9c" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating the Radius of Gyration of a Uniform Rectangular Laminar"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "28052605-ef85-5d61-b60d-35c652016958" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186278950} {:answer/id #uuid "30e535dc-d841-51b2-9346-6dd8f8151f9e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\sqrt{\\frac{7}{5}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186279019} {:answer/id #uuid "7d4a7fcf-e348-50c3-a268-aaa5fcf0d810" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\sqrt{\\frac{3}{2}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186279712} {:answer/id #uuid "cd62681a-f336-57f7-9271-562c7877f73a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\sqrt{5}}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186280402} {:answer/id #uuid "e5cb850d-af3a-58fe-9a74-754886c3ca4d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{2}{\\sqrt{3}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186280620}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "e5cb850d-af3a-58fe-9a74-754886c3ca4d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{2}{\\sqrt{3}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186280620} :answer-field/id #uuid "2fb299df-44bd-5725-bf66-0524bf139842" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186280921}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "c58b6231-e237-5de8-8e27-d0ade4f5cce7" :question/math-academy-id "q-163576" :question/problem "A rectangular plate of mass $M$ and uniform mass density occupies the region\n$D=\\{(x,y)\\,:\\,0\\le x\\le 2,\\,\\,0\\le y\\le 3\\}.$ Find the radius of gyration of the plate about the $y$-axis." :question/worked-solution "For a plane lamina in the shape of a region $D$ with mass $M$ and mass density function $\\lambda (x,y),$ we have the following definitions:\n\n- The radius of gyration ${R}_{x}$ about the $x$-axis is given by\n${R}_{x}=\\sqrt{\\frac{{I}_{x}}{M}},$\nwhere ${I}_{x}$ is the moment of inertia about the $x$-axis.\n\n- The radius of gyration ${R}_{y}$ about the $y$-axis is given by\n${R}_{y}=\\sqrt{\\frac{{I}_{y}}{M}},$\nwhere ${I}_{y}$ is the moment of inertia about the $y$-axis.\n\n- The radius of gyration ${R}_{0}$ about the origin is given by\n${R}_{0}=\\sqrt{\\frac{{I}_{0}}{M}},$\nwhere ${I}_{0}$ is the moment of inertia about the origin.\n\nThe moment of inertia about the $y$-axis is defined as\n\n$$\n{I}_{y}={∬}_{D}{x}^{2}\\lambda (x,y)\\,\\text{d}A,\n$$\n\nwhere $\\lambda (x,y)$ is the mass density function.\n\nThe area of the rectangular plate $D$ is $A=2\\cdot 3=6.$ Since the plate has uniform density, the mass density function is given by\n\n$$\n\\lambda (x,y)=\\frac{M}{A}=\\frac{M}{6}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the moment of inertia about the $y$-axis is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{I}_{y} & ={∬}_{D}{x}^{2}\\lambda (x,y)\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & =\\frac{M}{6}{\\int }_{0}^{3}{\\int }_{0}^{2}{x}^{2}\\,\\text{d}x\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & =\\frac{M}{6}{\\int }_{0}^{3}{[\\frac{1}{3}{x}^{3}]}_{0}^{2}\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & =\\frac{M}{6}{\\int }_{0}^{3}\\frac{1}{3}(8-0)\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & =\\frac{4M}{9}[y]_{0}^{3} \\\\  & =\\frac{4M}{9}\\cdot 3 \\\\  & =\\frac{4M}{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally,\n\n$$\n{R}_{y}^{2}=\\frac{4}{3}\\,⇒\\,{R}_{y}=\\sqrt{\\frac{4}{3}}=\\frac{2}{\\sqrt{3}}.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186281678 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186198417 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "2bfe2e3e-9d7b-5c53-8de8-2717237d3e9c" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating the Radius of Gyration of a Uniform Rectangular Laminar"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0d652bb7-2c2a-59df-a30e-8a26cac188ae" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2\\sqrt{\\frac{5}{3}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186278716} {:answer/id #uuid "78b8c404-1b74-574e-aaff-1cac4f74dbe5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\sqrt{\\frac{13}{3}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186279668} {:answer/id #uuid "a2f6880e-c432-5d49-a344-3611d4439c6f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2\\sqrt{10}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186280038} {:answer/id #uuid "bbd4a4e6-f500-5149-b052-7702a8b7faf6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{2\\sqrt{3}}{5}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186280245} {:answer/id #uuid "d680d34e-7009-583e-b502-5b6983be161b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\sqrt{\\frac{17}{5}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186280485}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "0d652bb7-2c2a-59df-a30e-8a26cac188ae" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2\\sqrt{\\frac{5}{3}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186278716} :answer-field/id #uuid "5840af3f-f19a-5638-befc-d037ec15bab6" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186280982}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "de217583-4705-57c2-81c7-b02676db7154" :question/math-academy-id "q-163582" :question/problem "A rectangular plate of mass $M$ and uniform mass density occupies the region\n$D=\\{(x,y)\\,:\\,1\\le x\\le 2,\\,\\,1\\le y\\le 3\\}.$ Find the radius of gyration of the plate about the origin." :question/worked-solution "For a plane lamina in the shape of a region $D$ with mass $M$ and mass density function $\\lambda (x,y),$ we have the following definitions:\n\n- The radius of gyration ${R}_{x}$ about the $x$-axis is given by\n${R}_{x}=\\sqrt{\\frac{{I}_{x}}{M}},$\nwhere ${I}_{x}$ is the moment of inertia about the $x$-axis.\n\n- The radius of gyration ${R}_{y}$ about the $y$-axis is given by\n${R}_{y}=\\sqrt{\\frac{{I}_{y}}{M}},$\nwhere ${I}_{y}$ is the moment of inertia about the $y$-axis.\n\n- The radius of gyration ${R}_{0}$ about the origin is given by\n${R}_{0}=\\sqrt{\\frac{{I}_{0}}{M}},$\nwhere ${I}_{0}$ is the moment of inertia about the origin.\n\nThe moment of inertia about the origin is defined as\n\n$$\n{I}_{0}={∬}_{D}\\lambda (x,y)({x}^{2}+{y}^{2})\\,\\text{d}A,\n$$\n\nwhere $\\lambda (x,y)$ is the mass density function.\n\nThe area of the rectangular plate $D$ is $A=1\\cdot 2=2.$ Since the plate has uniform density, the mass density function is given by\n\n$$\n\\lambda (x,y)=\\frac{M}{A}=\\frac{M}{2}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the moment of inertia about the origin is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{I}_{0} & ={∬}_{D}\\lambda (x,y)({x}^{2}+{y}^{2})\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & =\\frac{M}{2}{\\int }_{1}^{3}{\\int }_{1}^{2}{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}\\,\\text{d}x\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & =\\frac{M}{2}{\\int }_{1}^{3}{[\\frac{1}{3}{x}^{3}+x{y}^{2}]}_{x=1}^{x=2}\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & =\\frac{M}{2}{\\int }_{1}^{3}(\\frac{8}{3}+2{y}^{2}-\\frac{1}{3}-{y}^{2})\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & =\\frac{M}{2}{\\int }_{1}^{3}\\frac{7}{3}+{y}^{2}\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & =\\frac{M}{2}{[\\frac{7}{3}y+\\frac{1}{3}{y}^{3}]}_{1}^{3} \\\\  & =\\frac{M}{2}(7+9-\\frac{7}{3}-\\frac{1}{3}) \\\\  & =\\frac{M}{2}\\cdot \\frac{40}{3} \\\\  & =\\frac{20M}{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally,\n\n$$\n{R}_{0}^{2}=\\frac{20}{3}\\,⇒\\,{R}_{0}=\\sqrt{\\frac{20}{3}}=2\\sqrt{\\frac{5}{3}}.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186198663 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186198419 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "068d9714-bd1e-5036-a0c7-9be288831f52" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating Radii of Gyration Using Polar Coordinates"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "307a7ca4-01fa-5646-885b-a0e8867f3b6e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\sqrt{\\frac{5}{6}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186279016} {:answer/id #uuid "501aac95-5532-5856-a642-0d3b1d67f719" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\sqrt{\\frac{7}{10}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186279322} {:answer/id #uuid "5327eac7-a93d-5b6d-af9d-e6bb83813164" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\sqrt{\\frac{31}{35}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186279347} {:answer/id #uuid "9996b21a-d3a1-58ce-91cf-3cc1dfc91e45" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\sqrt{\\frac{17}{21}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186279948} {:answer/id #uuid "f72fd95a-5b27-5a58-83e0-471231a84783" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\sqrt{\\frac{11}{15}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186280756}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "5327eac7-a93d-5b6d-af9d-e6bb83813164" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\sqrt{\\frac{31}{35}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186279347} :answer-field/id #uuid "66c3c972-8140-526a-b8d9-d9d228cd316b" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186281010}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "b31c8b99-cc6d-5598-a2c8-85f537ed1a0d" :question/math-academy-id "q-163586" :question/problem "![](images/5b/5b8ddb36e814517af21d790374e1fb192141bd6ef0fd99e83a147c6ed5a62aea.png)\n\nA plate of mass $M$ occupies the region $D$ in the first quadrant bounded by the circles ${x}^{2}+{y}^{2}=1,$ ${x}^{2}+{y}^{2}=4,$ and the coordinate axes, as shown above. Its mass density at any point is given by $\\lambda (x,y)=\\frac{3}{7}My.$ Find the radius of gyration of the plate about the $y$-axis." :question/worked-solution "For a plane lamina in the shape of a region $D$ with mass $M$ and mass density function $\\lambda (x,y),$ we have the following definitions:\n\n- The radius of gyration ${R}_{x}$ about the $x$-axis is given by\n${R}_{x}=\\sqrt{\\frac{{I}_{x}}{M}},$\nwhere ${I}_{x}$ is the moment of inertia about the $x$-axis.\n\n- The radius of gyration ${R}_{y}$ about the $y$-axis is given by\n${R}_{y}=\\sqrt{\\frac{{I}_{y}}{M}},$\nwhere ${I}_{y}$ is the moment of inertia about the $y$-axis.\n\n- The radius of gyration ${R}_{0}$ about the origin is given by\n${R}_{0}=\\sqrt{\\frac{{I}_{0}}{M}},$\nwhere ${I}_{0}$ is the moment of inertia about the origin.\n\nIn polar coordinates, the region occupied by the plate is given by\n\n$$\nD=\\{(r,\\theta )\\,:\\,1\\le r\\le 2,\\,\\,0\\le \\theta \\le \\frac{\\pi }{2}\\}.\n$$\n\nThe moment of inertia about the $y$-axis, in polar coordinates, is defined as\n\n$$\n{I}_{y}={∬}_{D}\\lambda (r,\\theta ){r}^{3}{cos}^{2}⁡\\theta \\,\\text{d}r\\,\\text{d}\\theta ,\n$$\n\nwhere $\\lambda (r,\\theta )$ is the mass density function.\n\nAlso, the mass density in terms of polar coordinates is $\\lambda (r,\\theta )=\\frac{3}{7}Mr\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta .$\nTherefore, the moment of inertia about the $y$-axis is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{I}_{y} & ={∬}_{D}\\lambda (r,\\theta ){r}^{3}{cos}^{2}⁡\\theta \\,\\text{d}r\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & =\\frac{3}{7}M{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /2}{\\int }_{1}^{2}{r}^{4}{cos}^{2}⁡\\theta \\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta \\,\\text{d}r\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & =\\frac{3}{7}M({\\int }_{1}^{2}{r}^{4}\\,\\text{d}r)({\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /2}{cos}^{2}⁡\\theta \\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta \\,\\text{d}\\theta ) \\\\  & =\\frac{3}{7}M\\cdot \\frac{1}{5}{r}^{5}{|}_{1}^{2}\\cdot {[-\\frac{{cos}^{3}⁡\\theta }{3}]}_{0}^{\\pi /2} \\\\  & =\\frac{3}{7}M\\cdot (\\frac{32}{5}-\\frac{1}{5})\\cdot (-0+\\frac{1}{3}) \\\\  & =\\frac{3}{7}M\\cdot \\frac{31}{5}\\cdot \\frac{1}{3} \\\\  & =\\frac{31M}{35}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the radius of gyration about the $x$-axis is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{R}_{y} & =\\sqrt{\\frac{{I}_{y}}{M}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{\\frac{31M}{35}\\cdot \\frac{1}{M}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{\\frac{31}{35}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186370880 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186198421 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "aa0241de-b852-5c1f-962b-559e05edf39e" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating the Radius of Gyration of a Non-Uniform, Non-Rectangular Laminar"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "f293b5e9-65d5-536c-b18d-a76dc4e7ea80" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186370882} {:answer/id #uuid "2e26a64f-d68e-5522-ac57-78a01cfc8093" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186370883} {:answer/id #uuid "de7b89dc-f977-5e1a-9b52-09259a14b526" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\sqrt{\\frac{3}{5}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186370884} {:answer/id #uuid "6b112ea6-1937-5361-af39-bf68f7bc8dd2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186370885} {:answer/id #uuid "696ba733-0b46-5f03-b9f3-48ae1fe194cf" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{3}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186370886}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "696ba733-0b46-5f03-b9f3-48ae1fe194cf" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{3}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186370886} :answer-field/id #uuid "4a96fbcd-7761-58d9-ae0a-eb2b94c9e2c7" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186370881}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "defce080-8c65-59c1-a4eb-652286fe6d3f" :question/math-academy-id "q-38819" :question/problem "A plate of mass $M$ occupies the region $D$ bounded by the curve $y=\\sqrt{x},$ the line $x=1,$ and the $x$-axis. Its mass density at any point on the plate is given by $\\lambda (x,y)=4My.$ Find the radius of gyration of the plate about the $x$-axis." :question/worked-solution "For a plane lamina in the shape of a region $D$ with mass $M$ and mass density function $\\lambda (x,y),$ we have the following definitions:\n\n- The radius of gyration ${R}_{x}$ about the $x$-axis is given by\n${R}_{x}=\\sqrt{\\frac{{I}_{x}}{M}},$\nwhere ${I}_{x}$ is the moment of inertia about the $x$-axis.\n\n- The radius of gyration ${R}_{y}$ about the $y$-axis is given by\n${R}_{y}=\\sqrt{\\frac{{I}_{y}}{M}},$\nwhere ${I}_{y}$ is the moment of inertia about the $y$-axis.\n\n- The radius of gyration ${R}_{0}$ about the origin is given by\n${R}_{0}=\\sqrt{\\frac{{I}_{0}}{M}},$\nwhere ${I}_{0}$ is the moment of inertia about the origin.\n\nThe moment of inertia about the $x$-axis is defined as\n\n$$\n{I}_{x}={∬}_{D}{y}^{2}\\lambda (x,y)\\,\\text{d}A,\n$$\n\nwhere $\\lambda (x,y)$ is the mass density function. The region $D$ is a type I region with representation\n\n$$\nD=\\{(x,y)\\,:\\,0\\le x\\le 1,\\,\\,0\\le y\\le \\sqrt{x}\\}.\n$$\n\nHence, the moment of inertia about the $x$-axis is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{I}_{x} & ={∬}_{D}{y}^{2}\\lambda (x,y)\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{0}^{\\sqrt{x}}{y}^{2}\\cdot 4My\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =4M{\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{0}^{\\sqrt{x}}{y}^{3}\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =4M{\\int }_{0}^{1}{[\\frac{1}{4}{y}^{4}]}_{y=0}^{y=\\sqrt{x}}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =4M{\\int }_{0}^{1}\\frac{1}{4}{x}^{2}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =M{\\int }_{0}^{1}{x}^{2}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =M{[\\frac{1}{3}{x}^{3}]}_{0}^{1} \\\\  & =\\frac{M}{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the radius of gyration about the $x$-axis is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{R}_{x} & =\\sqrt{\\frac{{I}_{x}}{M}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{\\frac{M}{3}\\cdot \\frac{1}{M}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{\\frac{1}{3}} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{3}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}]}
